# <PROJECT NAME> — Spring Boot Backend — Development Rules

> Read and follow every rule here before starting **any** task — feature, bug fix, refactor,
> chore, one-line hot-fix, or a question whose answer leads to a code change. "It's only a small
> change" is never grounds to skip a rule.
>
> **A task ends only when the matching `docs/*.md` files reflect the change** (§21). Code compiling
> is not "done."
>
> Scope: the Spring Boot backend at the repo root (group `<GROUP>`, artifact `<ARTIFACT>`, Java 17,
> Maven, Spring Boot 4.x). Treat user/PII and any sensitive domain data as sensitive by default (§11).

## 0. Pre-Task Checklist

1. Read this file in full.
2. **Write a plan** — every class created/modified, its package, the approach — and wait for
   approval before writing code.
3. Check `docs/03-api-reference.md` so you don't duplicate an endpoint.
4. Check the feature package (`features/<feature>/`) before adding an entity/DTO/service/repository.
5. Grep for existing entities/repositories/mappers/utilities that already cover the need; extend
   rather than reinvent.
6. State the plan and wait for approval on any destructive/irreversible action (dropping/altering a
   table, editing an applied migration, force-push, deleting generated files).

## 1. Structure — feature-sliced

Packages by feature under `<basePackage>.features.<feature>`, each split into
`controller/ dto/ entity/ mapper/ repository/ service/`. Cross-cutting code lives in `common/`
(`audit/ base/ config/ exception/ exception_handler/ i18n/ response/ security/ validation/`); the
base package holds only the application entry point + a root health controller.

- Never add a feature directly under the base package; never create root-level
  `controller`/`service`/`repository`/`entity` god-packages spanning all features.
- Only create the subpackages a feature needs. A feature depends on `common/` freely and on another
  feature **only** through its service interface + DTOs — never its `repository/`/`entity/`.
- `common/` never imports from a feature. Default to package-private visibility.

## 2. Git commits

`<type>(<scope>): <short description>` — types `feat|fix|refactor|docs|chore|build|perf|security`,
scope = feature/infra area. Commit after each working unit once `./mvnw clean verify` passes.
Never commit: secrets/`.env`/`application-local.yml`, `target/`, a failing build, commented-out
code, or an edit to an already-applied migration. Never `--no-verify`, force-push a protected
branch, or `git reset --hard` without explicit instruction.

## 3. Walkthroughs

After every completed feature/fix/refactor, create `docs/walkthroughs/YYYY-MM-DD_<slug>.md`
(summary, files changed by package, API changes, schema changes, security impact, config, follow-ups)
and add a line to `docs/walkthroughs/README.md`.

## 4. Secrets & config

No credential/key/connection-string hardcoded — every one is `${ENV_VAR}`. Profiles:
`application.properties` (defaults + active profile), `application-dev`, `application-prod`
(env-sourced), gitignored `application-local`. Activate via `SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE`. Provide a
`.env.example` listing every variable. **Fail fast** on a missing required secret — never default a
security value to empty.

## 5. Database, entities & migrations

- Schema changes via **Flyway** (`V<n>__<desc>.sql`); `ddl-auto=validate` outside a local sandbox.
  **Never edit an applied migration** — ship a new one. One logical change per file. Zero-downtime:
  add-then-drop across two releases; a rename is drop+add.
- One `@Entity` per aggregate root, extending a `BaseEntity` `@MappedSuperclass`
  (`createdAt/updatedAt/createdBy/updatedBy` via JPA auditing). Standard Lombok shape
  (`@Getter @Setter @NoArgsConstructor(PROTECTED)`); **never `@Data` on an `@Entity`.** Identity
  equality by database id only. Bidirectional associations keep both sides in sync; default to LAZY.
- Persist absolute instants as `Instant` (UTC / `timestamptz`); `LocalDate`/`LocalTime` only for
  date/time-of-day concepts. Never format timestamps on the backend.
- Paginate any growable list (`Page<T>`); avoid N+1 with `@EntityGraph`/`JOIN FETCH`; index
  `WHERE`/`JOIN`/`ORDER BY` columns in the same migration.

## 6. Layered architecture

Controller → Service → Repository, no layer skipped. Controllers bind/validate/delegate to one
service method and wrap the result — no business logic or repository calls. Services hold logic +
`@Transactional`, take/return DTOs. Service interface + `*Impl` is the default. Repositories are
`JpaRepository`. **Constructor injection only** (`@RequiredArgsConstructor` on `final` fields).

## 7. DTOs & mapping

Request/response DTOs are Java `record`s. Validation lives on the request DTO, never the entity.
**Never return an `@Entity` from a controller.** A response DTO exposes only what the consumer needs.
Mappers are MapStruct `@Mapper(componentModel="spring")` interfaces (project-wide).

## 8. REST conventions

Base path `/api/v1/<resource>` (plural, kebab-case). Verbs map to intent. Status codes:
`200/201/400/401/403/404/409/429/500`. **Never `204`** — a void success is a `Success` envelope with
`data: null`. List endpoints paginate. Adding an endpoint updates `docs/03-api-reference.md` in the
same change.

## 9. Validation

Jakarta Bean Validation on request DTOs (`@Valid @RequestBody`). Cross-field/DB-dependent checks live
in the service and throw a typed exception. Custom constraints live in `common/validation/` and are
reused across features.

## 10. Error handling

A single global `@RestControllerAdvice` maps every exception to the `BaseResponseBody.Fail` envelope.
Domain exceptions in `common/exception/` extend `RuntimeException`; services throw them, never return
`null`. The client-facing message is generic and localized — **never a stack trace or raw message**;
detail is logged server-side only. A unique-constraint violation is caught and rethrown as a typed
`409`.

## 11. Security & PHI/PII

Authenticated by default; `permitAll()` explicit. Stateless JWT, CSRF disabled, `@EnableMethodSecurity`
+ `@PreAuthorize`. BCrypt passwords; a `@SecurePassword` constraint (max 72, complexity, HIBP check).
Refresh tokens stored as SHA-256 hashes with rotation + reuse detection; failures collapse to one
`InvalidCredentialsException`. CORS configured explicitly (never `@CrossOrigin("*")`). **No PHI/PII in
logs or URLs.** Every write attributable via `createdBy`/`updatedBy`. Prod enforces TLS. Secrets from
env vars (§4).

## 12. Logging

SLF4J via `@Slf4j`, parameterized (never concatenation), to console + a rolling file appender. Levels:
`error` (with the exception object), `warn`, `info`, `debug`. **No PHI at any level.**

## 13. Timestamps

`Instant`/UTC/`timestamptz` for absolute time; return raw ISO-8601, render client-side.

## 14. Configuration & beans

One `@Configuration` per concern under `common/config/`. Group properties behind
`@ConfigurationProperties`. Prefer auto-configuration over hand-rolled setup.

## 15. Transactions

`@Transactional` on service methods only; read-only reads use `readOnly = true`. Keep transactions
short (no HTTP/file-IO inside). Don't swallow exceptions in a way that defeats rollback.

## 16. Performance & caching

Redis cache with a fail-open `CacheErrorHandler`; named regions with explicit TTLs; **pair every
mutation with `@CacheEvict`.** Cache only read-heavy, rarely-changing data — never patient-specific
data without an invalidation story. Paginate; watch N+1; index.

## 17. Dead code & boundaries

Remove unused imports/methods/classes on sight (git preserves history). No feature imports another
feature's `Repository`/`@Entity`/package-private class. `common/` never imports a feature. Every PR
builds clean with `./mvnw clean verify`.

## 18. Style

Run a formatter (Spotless/Checkstyle) before commit if configured; otherwise match existing formatting
(4-space indent, one top-level type per file, braces same line). Deliberate Lombok; records for DTOs.
`PascalCase`/`camelCase`/`UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`. No wildcard imports.

## 19. Build & run

`./mvnw spring-boot:run` (local, Docker Compose Postgres/Redis) · `./mvnw clean verify` ·
`./mvnw clean package`. Never commit `target/`.

## 20. Check before building

Read `docs/01-project-overview.md`; for a feature read its section of `docs/03-api-reference.md`; for
schema read `docs/02-database-schema.md` + the latest migration; for auth read `docs/04-security.md`.
Extend/reuse existing code; only create new when the existing can't be extended without a breaking
change, and flag the trade-off in the walkthrough.

## 21. Post-task documentation

Every task ends with a docs update. Update, as applicable: `03-api-reference.md` (endpoints),
`02-database-schema.md` (migrations), `04-security.md` (roles/permissions/PHI fields),
`01-project-overview.md` (feature/integration/config), `05-localization.md` (messages/locales),
`docs/README.md` (new docs), and a walkthrough. Before committing:
`git status docs/` should show changes matching the task — if not, ask whether it really needed none.
